Include the standard headers that are used

edit_control.h calls std::strlen, std::memmove and std::memset,
list_box_control.cpp uses std::unique_ptr and std::make_unique, and
windows_item.cpp calls std::find, without including <cstring>, <memory> or
<algorithm>. MSVC's standard library reaches them through other headers;
libstdc++ does not, so GCC stops with "'memset' is not a member of 'std'" and
its siblings -- in every translation unit that includes edit_control.h.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

